        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449266",
          "text": "We are tasked with implementing a hash table with $ 500 $ slots using universal hashing. The table will store a set of student records, and you need to perform a lookup for a specific student's ID. There are already $3000$ student records in the table, and the student IDs are assumed to be uniformly distributed.\nIf we randomly select a student ID $ x $ for lookup, what is the expected number of collisions between $ x $ and the other student records already stored in the hash table, assuming the hash function is chosen randomly from a universal family of hash functions?",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "6:6",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,numerical-answers,hashing,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449248",
          "text": "<p>What is the time complexity of the following code if $bar(n)$ takes $O(\\log n)$ time to execute?<br> </p><pre data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">int i, j;\nfor (i = 1; i * i &lt;= n; i++)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for (j = 1; j &lt;= n; j = j * 2)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;bar(j);\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}</pre><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$O(n)$</li><li>$O(\\sqrt{n} (\\log n)^2)$</li><li>$O(\\sqrt{n} \\log n)$</li><li>$O(n^2 \\log n)$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,time-complexity,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449224",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following C function to compute the $n$-th term of a sequence:</p><pre data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">int sequence(int n) \n{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if (n &lt;= 1)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return n;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;int prev2 = 0;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;int prev1 = 1;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;int current = 0;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for (int i = 2; i &lt;= n; i++) \n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;current = prev1 + prev2;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;prev2 = prev1;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;prev1 = current;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return current;\n}</pre><p>sequence is defined as<strong>:</strong><br>$$<br>\\text{sequence}(n) =<br>\\begin{cases}<br>0 &amp; \\text{if } n = 0, \\\\<br>1 &amp; \\text{if } n = 1, \\\\<br>\\text{sequence}(n-1) + \\text{sequence}(n-2) &amp; \\text{if } n &gt; 1.<br>\\end{cases}<br>$$</p><p>Which of the following statements is/are TRUE about the above function? (Mark all correct choices)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>The function correctly computes the $n$-th term of the sequence for $n \\geq 0$.</li><li>The time complexity of the function is $O(n)$.</li><li>The function uses a recursive approach to calculate the sequence values.</li><li>The space complexity of the function is $O(1)$.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,identify-function,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449229",
          "text": "You are given an array $ A $ of $ n $ elements. The best possible algorithm to find two numbers in $ A $ whose difference is equal to a given threshold $ T $ will run in (assuming comparison-based sorting):<br /> <br />Which of the following options are correct for above question:                                                                         <br /><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> $O(n \\log n)$</li><li> $\\Omega(n \\log n)$</li> <li>$\\Omega( n^2\\log n)$</li>  <li>$O(n^2)$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,algorithm-design,time-complexity,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449238",
          "text": "<p>You are given an empty hash table of size $ 11 $ that uses open addressing with quadratic probing. The following sequence of keys is to be inserted:<br>$$ 34, 13, 91, 46, 68, 21 $$<br>The hash function used is $ h_1(x) = x \\% 11 $,and assume the value of constants equal to $2.$<br>Which of the inserted elements causes a collision? (Mark all the appropriate choices)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$ 89 $</li><li>$ 46 $</li><li>$ 68 $</li><li>$ 21 $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "b;c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,hashing,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449242",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements about searching algorithms are TRUE? (Mark all correct choices)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>The worst-case runtime of binary search is $ O(\\log n) $</li><li>A linear search can be used on unsorted arrays, while binary search requires the array to be sorted.</li><li>The time complexity of linear search is the same as that of a binary search for large inputs.</li><li>Binary search can be used on sorted arrays only, and it achieves $O(1)$ complexity in the best case when the target element is located at the middle.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,searching,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449272",
          "text": "Consider a min-heap implemented as an array, where the elements of the heap are inserted in the order $ 5, 12, 3, 19, 6, 15, 8, 7, 10, 4 $. The heap property is maintained after each insertion. The heap is implemented using zero-based indexing. Consider leaves height as $0$.\nWhat is the height of element $ 7 $ in this heap?",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "1:1",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,numerical-answers,min-heap,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449234",
          "text": "<p>You are given three matrices $ M_1, M_2, M_3 $ with dimensions as follows:</p><ul><li>$ M_1 $ is $ 10 \\times 20 $</li><li>$ M_2 $ is $ 20 \\times 30 $</li><li>$ M_3 $ is $ 30 \\times 40 $</li></ul><p>What is the minimum number of scalar multiplications needed to multiply these three matrices together?</p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "18000:18000",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,numerical-answers,matrix-chain-ordering,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449278",
          "text": "Consider an array of $ 9 $ integers that is being sorted using the heapsort algorithm. After the initial phase of the algorithm, which involves constructing the heap, which of the following arrangements could represent the array? (Select all that apply)<br /><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> $98\\;67\\;52\\;25\\;17\\;48\\;15\\;3\\;7$</li><li> $3\\;15\\;7\\;25\\;17\\;52\\;48\\;98\\;67$</li> <li>$98\\;52\\;67\\;17\\;48\\;15\\;3\\;25\\;7$</li>  <li>$3\\;7\\;17\\;25\\;52\\;15\\;48\\;67\\;98$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,heap-sort,multiple-selects,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449268",
          "text": "<p>Consider a binary tree that is almost a min-heap, with one node violating the min-heap property. Specifically, the node $20$ is violating the min-heap property. After applying the heapify procedure to restore the min-heap property, where will the node $20$ be located?</p><p><img alt=\"\" width=\"458\" height=\"232\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "5:5",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,numerical-answers,binary-heap,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449274",
          "text": "Consider the following functions:<br />$$<br />n \\log n, n^2, \\log n, n^{3/2}, \\log^2 n<br />$$<br />Which of the following is/are TRUE? (Mark all the appropriate choices)<br /><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> $ n \\log n = O(n^2) $  </li><li> $ n^{3/2} = O(n \\log n) $ </li> <li>$ \\log n = O(\\log^2 n) $ </li>  <li>$ n^2 = \\Omega(n \\log n) $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;c;d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,asymptotic-notations,multiple-selects,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449226",
          "text": "<p>Consider the code given below, which runs selection sort:<br>&nbsp;</p><pre data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">void selectionSort(int arr[], int size)\n{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;int i, j, minIndex, temp;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for (i = 0; i &lt; size - 1; i++)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;minIndex = i;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for (j = i + 1; j &lt; size; j++)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;if (________ )\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;minIndex = j;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;temp = arr[i];\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;arr[i] = arr[minIndex];\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;arr[minIndex] = temp;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}\n}</pre><p><br>Which condition is sufficient and will correctly implement the if statement to find the minimum element in the unsorted portion of the array?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$ \\text{arr}[j] &lt; \\text{arr}[minIndex] $</li><li>$ \\text{arr}[j] &gt; \\text{arr}[minIndex] $</li><li>$ \\text{arr}[j] == \\text{arr}[minIndex] $</li><li>$ \\text{arr}[j] \\leq \\text{arr}[minIndex] $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,insertion-sort,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449246",
          "text": "<p>The return value, time complexity, and space complexity of the following code are:</p><pre data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">int bar(int n)\n{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;int a = 0;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;for (int i = 1; i &lt;= n; i++)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;{\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a += i * i;\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;}\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;return a;\n}</pre><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$ \\Theta(n^3), \\Theta(n), O(1) $</li><li>$ \\Theta(n), \\Theta(\\log n), O(1) $</li><li>$ \\Theta(n), \\Theta(n), O(n) $</li><li>$ \\Theta(n^2), O(n), O(1) $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,time-complexity,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449264",
          "text": "Consider the following array that is being sorted using the Quick Sort algorithm, where the last element is chosen as the pivot during each partitioning step. <br />Initial array:  <br />$$ 15, 7, 25, 12, 20, 10 $$<br />Which of the following is/are the possible array contents after the second pass of partitioning (using the last element as the pivot)?<br /><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> $ 7, 10, 12, 15, 20, 25 $</li><li> $ 7, 10, 12, 15, 25, 20 $</li> <li>$ 7, 10, 12, 20, 15, 25 $</li>  <li>$ 7, 15, 10, 25, 12, 20 $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,quick-sort,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449254",
          "text": "<p>You are given an empty hash table of size $ 7 $ that uses open addressing with quadratic probing. The following sequence of keys is to be inserted: &nbsp;<br>$$<br>34, 20, 15, 8, 25<br>$$ &nbsp;<br>The hash function is defined as: $h(x) = x \\% 7$<br>Considering the value of constants equal to $1,$ which keys will cause a collision during insertion?. (Mark all the correct choices)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$ 8 $<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>$ 15 $<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>$ 20 $<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>$ 34 $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;c",
