        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449276",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is/are correct about huffman coding?(Mark all the appropriate choices)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Huffman coding generates the optimal prefix code for a set of symbols based on their frequencies.</li><li>The result of the huffman coding algorithm is a binary tree.</li><li>Huffman coding assigns shorter codes to symbols that appear more frequently and longer codes to symbols that appear less frequently.</li><li>If input array is sorted based on frequencies, then Time complexity of standard huffman coding is linear.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;c;d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,huffman-coding,multiple-selects,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449280",
          "text": "<p>Suppose you are given the following set of keys to insert into a hash table that holds exactly $12$ values: $22, 39, 56, 71, 18, 91, 44, 83.$ Which of the following best demonstrates the contents of the hash table after all the keys have been inserted using linear probing and the multiplication method with $ h(k) = \\lfloor 12 \\times (k \\times 0.5 \\mod 1) \\rfloor $ as the hash function?<br> </p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$ 22\\; 56\\; 18\\; 44\\; -\\; -\\; 39\\; 71\\; 91\\; 83\\; -\\; -$</li><li>$ 56\\; -\\; 39\\; 22\\; 71\\; 18\\; 91\\; 44\\; 83\\; -\\; -\\; -$</li><li>$ 22\\; 56\\; 18\\; 44\\; -\\; 39\\; 71\\; 91\\; 83\\; -\\; -\\; -$</li><li>$ 56\\; 39\\; -\\; 22\\; 71\\; -\\; 44\\; 91\\; 18\\; 83\\; -\\; -$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,hashing,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449262",
          "text": "<p>Given an array of $ n $ elements, you are tasked with designing an algorithm to find the median element in the given unsorted array. What is the worst case time complexity of the best such algorithm?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$ O(n \\log n) $</li><li>$ O(n) $</li><li>$ O(\\log n) $</li><li>$ O(n^2) $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,time-complexity,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449282",
          "text": "<p>Consider two algorithms, $A$ and $B.$ Algorithm $A$ has a better space complexity (uses less memory) but takes more time, while algorithm $B$ has a better time complexity (is faster) but consumes more memory. Which of the following statements is/are TRUE? (Mark all that apply)<br>&nbsp;</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>For very large input sizes, algorithm $A$ may outperform algorithm $B$ due to its better space efficiency, despite being slower.</li><li>Algorithm $A's$ lower memory usage could make it more practical for applications with limited memory, even though it is slower.</li><li>Algorithm $B$ will always be faster than algorithm $A$ for any input size.</li><li>If memory usage is not a concern, algorithm $B$ will likely be the better choice for most input sizes due to its faster execution.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "b;d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,asymptotic-notations,multiple-selects,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449236",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is/are TRUE? (Mark all the appropriate choices)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>The time complexity for inserting an element into a balanced binary search tree is $O(\\log n)$ in the worst case.</li><li>The minimum number of comparisons required to sort a list of $8$ elements using merge sort is $O(n \\log n)$.</li><li>A complete binary tree of height $h$ can have at most $2^h - 1$ nodes(where height of root node $= 0$).</li><li>The time complexity for deleting the root element from a max-heap of $n$ elements is $O(\\log n)$.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449244",
          "text": "<p>You are tasked with purchasing items from a vending machine. The vending machine has $5$ different items available for sale where each item is sufficiently available, with the following prices:</p><ul><li>Item $A:$ $Rs. 500$</li><li>Item $B:$ $Rs. 200$</li><li>Item $C:$ $Rs. 150$</li><li>Item $D:$ $Rs. 100$</li><li>Item $E:$ $Rs. 50$</li></ul><p>Each time you choose an item to purchase, you are charged an additional service fee of $Rs. 10,$ which is the same for each item, regardless of its price. You are required to buy exactly $Rs. 1000$ worth of items.<br>What is the minimum service fee you would have to pay to purchase items worth exactly $Rs. 1000?$</p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "20:20",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,numerical-answers,dynamic-programming,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449258",
          "text": "Imagine you have a hash table with $ 15 $ slots, and you store $ 8 $ records in it using open addressing with linear probing. Assume that the hash function distributes keys uniformly, so the probability of any key being hashed into a particular slot is $ \\dfrac{1}{15} $. What is the probability that a specific slot contains at least one of the $ 8 $ keys (rounded to $2$ decimal places)?",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "0.53:0.54",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,numerical-answers,hashing,open-addressing,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449256",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following C function and an input array to it as $ [2, 5, 8, 11] $ and $ \\text{len} $ as $ 4 $. The return value of the function will be:</p><pre data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\">int bar(int arr[], int len) \n{\n    int result = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; len; i++) \n    {\n        result *= (arr[i] + i%2 + 1);\n    }\n    return result;\n}</pre><p> </p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "2457:2457",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,numerical-answers,identify-function,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449231",
          "text": "<p>You are given the following array $ A = \\{12, -5, 3, -1, 8, -2, 9, -6, 4, 5, -8, 2, 6, -7, 7\\} $, and the maximum subarray sum of this array is $ 27 $.<br>Which of the following subarrays from the given options has the same maximum sum of $ 27 $?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$ \\{12, -5, 3, -1, 8, -2, 9, -6, 4, 5\\} $</li><li>$ \\{-5, 3, -1, 8, -2, 5, 7\\} $</li><li>$ \\{12, -5, 3, -1, 8, -2, 9, -6, 4, 5, -8, 2, 6\\} $</li><li>$ \\{8, -2, 5, 7, -4\\} $</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,algorithm-design,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "449270",
          "text": "We are tasked with sorting a large set of product records based on their product prices. The records are already sorted by product categories in ascending order, but the sorting of records by category is not important for this particular task. The requirement is to sort the records by price, without worrying about maintaining the order of records within the same category.  <br />Which of the following sorting algorithms is/are most appropriate for this task?                                                       <br /><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li> Merge Sort </li><li> Counting Sort </li> <li>Quick Sort </li>  <li>Insertion Sort</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "go2026-algorithms-shallow-1,sorting,one-mark",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
